jobs.description:
Are you looking for a varied role in the manufacturing industry? Then we’re looking for you to work for a client in Ittervoort. This is a position as an operator on the mixing line, working in a 3-shift rotation. This means you’ll be responsible for assembling orders. You’ll ensure that the logistics process runs smoothly and that everything is put together properly. Your daily responsibilities will include the following:

- You’ll create the correct combinations and place the products together in the packaging;
- You’ll check that the packages are complete and undamaged as they’re loaded onto the pallets;
- Occasionally moving products with a forklift.

This is a three-shift position, Monday through Friday. You will work the following shifts: 5:54 a.m.–2:00 p.m., 1:54 p.m.–10:00 p.m., 9:54 p.m.–6:00 a.m. (7.36 paid hours).

- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You have experience with production work;
- You have experience operating a forklift.
- Would you like to further your career in production? Then we’re looking for you!

Do you want to be the driving force behind the production of the tastiest Oriental dishes?🍜 As a Line Operator at this leading food producer, you ensure everything runs like a well-oiled machine! Together with an enthusiastic team, you work with passion every day to deliver top quality. Ready to take charge ,and boost your career? This is your chance! Apply now, and I'll contact you within one working day!

What we offer
- Monthly salary from € 2,869 (40h)!
- Extra 8% holiday pay & 3% bonus!
- Great disounts on oriental meals!
- Weekly salary payments!
- Unlimited online training & growth!
- A warm, informal shift team!

Who you are
Are you a real leader who keeps their cool when things get busy? You have a sharp eye for quality and you're not afraid to take responsibility. Safety and hygiene are second nature to you! You are the perfect match if you meet the following:

- You have an MBO level 3 degree or similar experience;
- You have at least 2 years of experience as an operator in the food industry (required);
- You speak English or Dutch fluently;
- You are available for 40 hours a week in two shifts;
- You have your own transport to reach the location in Oss.

What will you do
As our new Line Operator, you are the captain of the production line!🚢 You don't just watch the machines; you lead your team to success every single day. From the moment you start your shift, you ensure everything runs like a well-oiled machine. You'll be coaching your colleagues, spotting any deviations in the process before they even happen, and making sure the delicious meals are top-quality. It's a responsible job where your technical skills and leadership really makes a difference!
Your main goals:

- Leading and coaching your enthusiastic team to reach the daily targets;
- Guiding the production process and ensuring a safe, hygienic environment (HACCP);
- Performing first-line maintenance to keep the line running smoothly;
